WEBVTT

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:16.620
"Koro Sensei Quest"

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:26.040
"Nagisa"

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:27.710
"Karma"

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:28.710
"Kaede"

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:30.050
"Isogai" "Maehara"

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:32.720
"Rio" "Okuda" "Sugino" "Kanzaki"

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:34.220
"Itona" "Ritsu"

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:35.720
"Chiba" "Hayami" "Hinata" "Meg"

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:38.220
"Justice" "Toka" "Takebayashi" "Hinano"

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:40.220
"Muramatsu" "Kirara" "Yoshida" "Terasaka"

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:42.220
"Sugaya" "Fuwa" "Mimura" "Hara" "Okajima"

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.230
"Karasuma" "Irina"

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:00.030
"Bye-Bye, Big Bad"

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:07.540
After we beat the Big Bad, I wanna be an artist.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:09.960
It'd be awesome if I got a post at the palace!

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:12.960
Me, I'd like to be a theater promoter.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:15.260
My goal is to be
the world's top entertainment king!

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:16.930
Well, I... I...

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:20.300
I'll live with the world's beauties
at my beck and call with <i>my</i> prize money--

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:23.140
for as long as I live! My whole life long!

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.890
Okajima's such a perv.

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:26.560
Looks that way.

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:34.400
Sugaya! Mimura! Okajima!

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:39.280
I'd love to take a trip around the world.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:43.120
I'd come to know all kinds of people
and different cultures.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:44.950
Sounds like you, Nakamura.

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:48.920
I'd like to build something with my prize money.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:50.670
A place for kids with nowhere to go.

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:51.460
Oh!

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:55.880
Nice! And I can teach them athletics!

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:57.380
Fantastic!

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:06.390
--Okano!
--Kurahashi! Nakamura!

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:09.730
My real name is Justice.

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:12.400
Having such a weird name used to bug me,

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.230
but now I'm proud of it.

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:18.290
So no more Masayoshi--I'm Justice from now on!

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:23.330
Masayoshi!

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:23.370
"E Class: 21 left"

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:29.750
Chiba!

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:31.420
I'll handle this. You go on ahead!

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:33.130
But that means...

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:34.580
Look out, Chiba!

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:38.470
Rinka!

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:40.340
Hurry. There's no time.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:43.340
Now go! Go--and beat the Big Bad!

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:48.770
Take my six.

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:49.520
Roger.

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:52.560
You won't get past us--
not as long as we have ammo!

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:56.820
"E Class: 19 left"

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:59.780
--What the--?!
--The walls are closing in!

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:01.360
I'll handle this!

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:02.450
--Hara!
--Hara!

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:03.570
See...

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:06.580
...I'd kept on eating and eating all this time

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:08.660
for exactly this moment!

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:10.290
Thirds!

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:15.460
I can't hold out for very long!

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:18.130
Go--for the whole world's sake!

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.590
"E Class: 18 left"

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:21.180
The ceiling's going to fall! Hurry!

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:26.140
The good Terasaka!

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.100
Now leave it to me!

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.970
"I'll hold it off!"

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.930
"Our time together sure was fun!"

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.280
It was a pleasant time spent with you all!

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:36.360
You guys...

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:36.360
"You guys..."

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:38.820
You're not the only one who gets to show off!

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:41.320
We're pals, ain't we?

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:44.320
A bunch of misfits like us? Bring it on!

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:50.580
"E Class: 14 left"

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:54.920
I'll clear a path--
you just take your time, mmkay?

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:56.420
We'll come, too!

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.170
What a man!

00:03:58.170 --> 00:03:59.840
They're coming from behind!

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:02.510
--Kanzaki!
--Kanzaki!

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:04.050
I'll handle this.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:06.720
Not alone, you won't, Kanzaki!

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:10.020
Sugi-Strike!

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.200
I can't use my bug!

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:14.560
"Bug: Delayed magic activation"

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:16.150
Sugino?

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:17.400
Huh?

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:20.480
Ah!

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:23.530
The magic he cast
in episode 3 just now activated!

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.030
"Episode 3"? What's that?

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:30.120
Wait... But he didn't cast it just once, did he?

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:35.040
Hmph. So this is <i>that</i> part.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.230
Where we get picked off
one by one--for Reasons.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.340
"E Class: 8 left"

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:45.880
Takebayashi... I... I can't take much more.

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:48.640
Thank you. I leave the rest to you.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:50.140
What are you saying?

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:52.430
What happened to us
all beating the Big Bad together?

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:53.850
Purge!

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:05.450
Takebayashi...

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:11.120
"E Class: 7 left"

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:08.910
Such good people--all of 'em!

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:11.620
We won't let their sacrifices be in vain!

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:13.750
--Ah!
--Ah!

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:15.660
--Isogai!
--Maehara!

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.000
--But you <i>just said</i>...!
--But you <i>just said</i>...!

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:18.920
"E Class: 5 left"

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:21.380
So there are only five of us left...

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:23.210
This day had come at last:

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:26.320
the final battle between
the E Class and the Big Bad!

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:36.060
--♪ The wind blows ♪

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.480
--<i>Whaaat</i>?!
--♪ The wind blows ♪

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:43.740
--♪ And presses on my shoulder ♪

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:45.530
--What are you <i>doing</i>?!
--♪ And presses on my shoulder ♪

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:47.860
--It's a graduation ceremony--mine.
--♪ Ah, the road I must follow ♪

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:48.820
--<i>Yours</i>?!
--♪ Ah, the road I must follow ♪

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:51.240
--I wanted to sing, too.
--♪ Ah, the road I must follow ♪

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.370
--Who cares?!
--♪ Ah, the road I must follow ♪

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.410
--Congratulations, me!
--♪ Now lays ahead of you ♪

00:05:54.700 --> 00:06:00.380
"Be happy"

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:59.210
--Be happy!
--♪ Now lays ahead of you ♪

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:02.800
What <i>is</i> all this?

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:03.800
The truth is...

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:07.880
The Big Bad,
choosing to be involved in education.

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.390
I had high hopes for you...

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:14.850
But you've just been fooling around,
like one of your students.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:19.440
--You're fired.
--What?! Fired, just like that?

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:21.060
Yes: fired.

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:26.400
I meant well, but it seems
our warm communication has backfired!

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:30.160
I should have just put my all
into being mean and nasty!

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.660
You're mad at the wrong thing.

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:36.620
And so, I thought I'd go out with
a big bang of a graduation ceremony.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:38.870
Our friends sacrificed themselves for <i>that</i>?!

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:42.000
He's right! If this is a joke,
it's gone way too far!

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.360
Well, in that case,
it just so happens all those traps--

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:45.840
They're fine!

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.260
<i>What</i>?!

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:49.300
"A Lv. 99 Terasaka appeared!"

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:49.300
<i>Who</i>?!

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.430
"E Class: 5 left"

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.550
I rescued 'em all.

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:52.890
"E Class: 29 left"

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:52.890
What happened?!

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:54.720
After I got swapped with that fake,

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:57.600
I lived through day after day of sheer hell

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:00.030
just to escape the dungeon I got left in.

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:02.860
Now I'm level 99.

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:04.750
Before!

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:08.780
After!

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:10.030
What <i>happened</i>?!

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:15.030
<i>And</i> I got to master my bug, the Slither!

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:15.030
"Bug: Magic turns liquid"

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:16.410
It's all slithery.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:18.000
"Saved by Slither"

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:18.330
Yeah. It's slithery.

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:19.580
That Slither is amazing.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:21.960
But being slithery is <i>my</i> thing!

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:25.880
All right, Big Bad... say your prayers!

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:30.630
Th-Those were all dummy traps!
No one was ever going to get hurt!

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:33.590
I know! Won't you join me?

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:34.760
Half the world will be yours!

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:37.260
And I might actually
be your dad! <i>Everyone's</i> dad!

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:39.850
And this isn't even my final form!

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:40.930
And uh, um... Oh, yeah!

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:42.100
What's he doing?

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:43.770
It's a Big Bad thing.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:47.190
What an attack!
Can't get a comeback in edgewise!

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:48.030
"Itona took damage!"

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:48.030
It's working?!

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:51.490
At this rate, Terasaka might just kill him.

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:54.070
What do we do? Koro Sensei'll die!

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:56.530
Uh, wasn't that the whole point?

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:01.960
Oh, no, Mr. Big Bad!

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:04.630
Those traps were pushed so far past their limit

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:06.710
that the castle is starting to collapse!

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:08.500
What are <i>you</i> doing here, sis?!

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:13.510
That's the only exit!

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:16.380
Aw! All because you said
the Big Bad has to wait

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:18.310
in the deepest part of the castle!

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:19.720
So it's <i>your</i> fault!

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:22.060
Nagisa...

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.940
We need your power at a time like this.

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:25.520
Eh?

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:27.480
Your bug, Nagisa.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:29.730
We don't know what'll happen!

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:31.820
We <i>don't</i> know what'll happen.

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:36.320
But surely, if <i>you're</i> behind it,
it will work for good.

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:38.590
<i>That</i> is your power.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:42.500
It's our only hope! We have to try!

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.370
If I wind up killing my students,

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:47.130
I'll be practically erased from society!

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:48.250
Sir...

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:54.090
My... my power!

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:05.730
"The adventure log has vanished"

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:09.400
How do you do?

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:13.280
I'm the Big Bad,
and as of today, I'm your teacher.

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:14.030
Eh?

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:17.360
Wait a second! Why are we
starting over from the beginning?

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:20.910
Huh? I feel like... I remember! Kind of...

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:23.580
Aw, man! We gotta do this <i>again</i>?

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:26.790
Wait! <i>What</i>?! Did my bug do this?

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:29.750
It would seem this is one of its effects.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:32.630
I'm just glad I'm back to before I was fired.

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:34.130
So we're doing this?

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:39.180
You can fail. You can try and try again.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:42.140
Aim to be fine upstanding warriors.

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:51.070
"New Game +"

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:51.070
I'm so happy to be able
to teach you all like this again.

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:54.030
Now, starting with whoever's ready...

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:55.820
Come and get me!

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:58.110
Yes, sir!
